Possible spoilers...



S'okay?  Nothing connected, just a few points and questions:

I remember somebody mentioning that ring of conflict was too powerful;
I think ditto for the magic flute, although it's harder to find.  I used
it on the castle level and got everybody behind the drawbridge except for
a Lich or two.  And this ain't any wand-of-sleep 40 winks stuff either,
it's practically euthanasia.  I didn't even take it with me to Hell because
I missed having things fight back.

And I think the same may have to be said for cockatrice corpses.  I cleaned
out Vlad's castle without having to take a second hit at anything.  Maybe
this should be less effective at actually hitting things, or the transformation
should be slower (the way it is for the player) to tone it down some.

I'm a diehard polypiler, but I gotta admit, it's too much when you run into
a couple of bones levels in a row.  Maybe if you couldn't polymorph other
wands into wands of polymorph, just to make it less abusive?

Do any of the demon-lords or the Wizard destroy armor?  I remember that being
a problem in one of the earlier incarnations of the game, but haven't noticed
it happening in this version.  Now that was REALLY scary.

What is it that makes me rip up scrolls I'm trying to write with a magic marker?
Is it luck? Is it intelligence, wisdom, strength, experience?  I thought I'd
checked all that out.  Mmmmm, maybe I knew they were blank paper (from dipping
in fountains) but didn't actually identify them...

That's all.  Happy hacking, everybody. -SGroup 



